  "notes": "COMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n・{本音|ほんね}を{吐露|とろ}する (reveal one's true feelings)\n・{心情|しんじょう}を{吐露|とろ}する (disclose one's emotions)\n・{胸|むね}の{内|うち}を{吐露|とろ}する (reveal what is in one's heart)\n・{不満|ふまん}を{吐露|とろ}する (express one's dissatisfaction)\n\nA literary and somewhat formal word. The object is always something emotional or personal — feelings, frustrations, innermost thoughts. Common in news reporting, interviews, and literary prose.",
